## Highlights
An ultrasensitive competitive electrochemical immunosensor for MD detection was constructed by using AuNPs as GCE modifier and hemin $@$ MOFs/AuPt- $\mathbf{\nabla}\cdot\mathbf{A}\mathbf{b}_{2}$ -HRP/HRP as bioprobes.
A linear calibration curve of MD ranged from $0.1~\mathrm{{ng}~\mathrm{{mL}^{-1}}}$ to $50\mathrm{\ng\mL^{-1}}$ was obtained with LOD as low as $0.045~\mathrm{ng~mL^{-1}}$ .
A multiple signal amplification strategy was triggered by the co-synergistic effect of hemin $@$ MOFs, AuPt and HRP to generate the signal current.
The proposed immunosensor with high sensitivity, good selectivity and acceptable stability shows a great potential for sensitive detection of small molecule drug residues.
